       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the labeled maximum for metformin, and I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Order as written:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** The maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as no more than 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg PO twice daily\n- Something else\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and include a note for the order, and I'll enter it as written."
